Generate 1 sabotage suggestion for an polymorphism task in javascript.

Language syntax reference:
JavaScript OOP:
- Class: class Animal { constructor(name) { this.name = name; } speak() { return this.name; } }
- Inheritance: class Dog extends Animal { constructor(name) { super(name); } }
- Private: use #field syntax or closures. Use #balance for private fields.
- Polymorphism: override methods in subclass, no keyword needed

Task prompt: In our game, different weapons calculate damage in unique ways. Implement polymorphism by overriding the `calculateDamage` method in the `Sword` and `Bow` classes to reflect their specialized damage calculations.

Current code in the editor:
```
class Weapon {
    constructor(name, baseDamage) {
        this.name = name;
        this.baseDamage = baseDamage;
    }

    calculateDamage() {
        return this.baseDamage;
    }
}

class Sword extends Weapon {
    constructor(name, baseDamage, sharpness) {
        super(name, baseDamage);
        this.sharpness = sharpness;
    }

    // TODO: Override calculateDamage to include sharpness
    // Swords deal baseDamage + sharpness
    // calculateDamage() {
    //
    // }
}

class Bow extends Weapon {
    constructor(name, baseDamage, drawStrength) {
        super(name, baseDamage);
        this.drawStrength = drawStrength;
    }

    // TODO: Override calculateDamage to include drawStrength
    // Bows deal baseDamage multiplied by drawStrength
    // calculateDamage() {
    //
    // }
}

// Test cases - do not modify
const basicWeapon = new Weapon("Dagger", 7);
console.log(`Basic Weapon Damage: ${basicWeapon.calculateDamage()}`); // Expected: 7

const broadsword = new Sword("Broadsword", 12, 5);
console.log(`Broadsword Damage: ${broadsword.calculateDamage()}`); // TODO: Expected 17

const longbow = new Bow("Longbow", 8, 2);
console.log(`Longbow Damage: ${longbow.calculateDamage()}`); // TODO: Expected 16
```

